--
N5008 [class.mi]/3-4: a class can be an indirect non-virtual base more than
once; each occurrence is a distinct subobject ("struct D : virtual B,
virtual C", with B and C both derived non-virtually from A, has two A
subobjects).  Only an ambiguous name or conversion is ill-formed
([class.member.lookup]/6, [conv.ptr]/3), not the class itself; `d.B::i'
and `d.C::i' name one each.  The front end rejects the class definition
("non-virtual base class tag-A inherited multiple times").
Multiple_Inheritance3 (CORE, from the 2012 CVS tests, "we do not allow
this") pins that rejection; g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept its program.
Found by the round-163c audit of descs that expect a rejection.
Reference compilers: g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it
fails only its WRONG assertion.  Pre-existing (round-162 snapshot bin51).
